Declined, with the reason, per signoff-driver step 5.

Third-party licence notices are absent from the binary channels. Every
review-deps reviewer across every round graded it minor: the blocking
licence band is a copyleft dependency in a permissive project, and this
change removes the only one. Tracked as a follow-up, and it should land
before the packages get wide.

`diataxis` and `mdstore-core` are first-party crates published days
before this commit. Both replace hand-rolled code rather than a
consensus library, both are maintained, and moving `mdstore` off a git
revision is what makes a crates.io publish possible at all.

The vocabulary is a half-finished rename: tracker, store and repository
reach one workflow. Reviewers named it independently in both rounds and
all graded it minor. The `store` command group, `stores.yml` and the
`root_store:` output key are public surface, so the rename belongs in
its own change.

`issue create` and `init` write and print nothing. Two reviewers put it
close to the blocking line and both declined it, because the arms are
byte-identical to main and this change does not touch them.

